Precision Machine Design — MIT 2.75, Fall 2001 (@mech-mit-precision: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_1NC9D5QBNMR4S8THM7KFNG32KB
Martin Culpepper and Alexander Slocum. [Graduate course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-75-precision-machine-design-fall-2001/) · [Selected lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-75-precision-machine-design-fall-2001/pages/lecture-notes/).

Use the precision-design account for constraints, error budgets, bearings, actuators and integration under stated functional requirements. The public lecture page provides selected exact/quasi-exact constraint, adjustable/flexible constraint and milestone material. The course also provides project and assignment context.

The index was inspected on 30 October 2026. It is a historical graduate offering, not a claim about the current meaning of MIT course number 2.75. Available notes are selected rather than a complete recorded curriculum. Preserve OCW CC BY-NC-SA and component notices. Use the fuller Slocum book and additional primary methods where the public course material leaves a gap.

